PROCGREP(1)                    ZOAU Command Syntax                   PROCGREP(1)

NAME
	procgrep - Search for a string across the proclib concatenation.

SYNOPSIS

	procgrep [-dhinv] <str> <dataset-pattern>

	-d
		Print out debug messages.

	-h
		Display syntax help.

	-i
		Ignore case.

	-n
		Display line numbers.

	-v
		Print out verbose command information.

DESCRIPTION

	Search for a string across the proclib concatenation.

DATASET PATTERNS

	The following rules apply to <dataset-pattern>:

	The high-level qualifier (HLQ) must be specified in full.
	An asterisk (*) matches any sequence of characters.
	A question mark (?) matches a single character.

EXAMPLES

	Search for rdtd (case sensitive) across the proclib concatenation.

		procgrep rdtd

	Search for Hello (case insensitive) across the proclib concatenation,
	displaying line numbers.

		procgrep -in Hello

EXIT VALUES

	0
		Success

	Other
		Error, see message for details

SEE ALSO

	parmgrep(1)
